{"assets":["/statement-assets/271585868f7987bcf7fc69fa49896eb251dd4e959062e17647bdeab0048d8583.png","/statement-assets/908bc20beaec6b8cec833778ec862b0eb4476d6750d5b5811f6ed248badfb907.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"196","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Infinite Maze"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We've got a rectangular "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n × m"},{"kind":"text","text":"-cell maze. Each cell is either passable, or is a wall (impassable). A little boy found the maze and cyclically tiled a plane with it so that the plane became an infinite maze. Now on this plane cell "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x, y)"},{"kind":"text","text":" is a wall if and only if cell "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/271585868f7987bcf7fc69fa49896eb251dd4e959062e17647bdeab0048d8583.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" is a wall."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In this problem "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/908bc20beaec6b8cec833778ec862b0eb4476d6750d5b5811f6ed248badfb907.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" is a remainder of dividing number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" by number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The little boy stood at some cell on the plane and he wondered whether he can walk infinitely far away from his starting position. From cell "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x, y)"},{"kind":"text","text":" he can go to one of the following cells: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x, y - 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x, y + 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x - 1, y)"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x + 1, y)"},{"kind":"text","text":", provided that the cell he goes to is not a wall."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two space-separated integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n, m ≤ 1500"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the height and the width of the maze that the boy used to cyclically tile the plane."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" characters — the description of the labyrinth. Each character is either a \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"#"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", that marks a wall, a \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", that marks a passable cell, or an \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"S"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", that marks the little boy's starting point. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The starting point is a passable cell. It is guaranteed that character \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"S"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" occurs exactly once in the input."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without the quotes), if the little boy can walk infinitely far from the starting point. Otherwise, print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"No"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without the quotes)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5 4\n##.#\n##S#\n#..#\n#.##\n#..#\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"Yes\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5 4\n##.#\n##S#\n#..#\n..#.\n#.##\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"No\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample the little boy can go up for infinitely long as there is a \"clear path\" that goes vertically. He just needs to repeat the following steps infinitely: up, up, left, up, up, right, up."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second sample the vertical path is blocked. The path to the left doesn't work, too — the next \"copy\" of the maze traps the boy."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"196B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/196/problem/B"}